/-
Fmt/Toy1Files.lean: test data for the byte format of proofs: two honest proof files of a small toy
of this library's own and 19 altered ones, as bytes.

The toy was made to rehearse a run. Definitions, and tests (#guard): the sizes; the 21 files differ
from one another; the honest file's hash under the number 168; seven copies differ from it in one
byte; the copy that is cut and the one that is lengthened. Made by a program from the files and from
the table that came with them. The data are made-up toy data: no model and no weights. No Mathlib.
This library's own toy, not the programs'. The protocol is a toy of this library's own for a
rehearsal of the run; the files were made outside Lean by the format page's own reference program
(its Python twin), at another edition of the page than the one that ships. No file here comes
from the programs (the C++
implementation that comes with this Lean code).
The toy. The second field; one tree of depth 4 (16 columns of one element of the extension field
each), number 0, made in the run; a leaf's salt has 40 bytes; a nonce 8 bytes; the chain's label is
7, with random bytes; the configuration has one public file; the claim c = (1, 2, 3). Round 1: the
prover sends the root; 8 bits of work; the verifier draws 3 positions. Round 2: the prover sends s;
the verifier's message is empty. The decision: s = c + the sum of the symbols at the listed
positions.
A file, in order: the random bytes (32); the root (32); the nonce (8); for each listed position, in
increasing order, its column (24) and its salt (40); the given digests of the walk (32 each); s
(24).

Main names:
  `Toy1.honest`, `Toy1.honest2`: the two honest files (the second: another row, so another root and
    another draw).
  `Toy1.alt01` and those after it: the altered files; what was altered stands at each, in the words
    of the table that came with them. "RE-CUT": opening and s are made anew for the positions that
    the altered chain draws, so that a lenient reader (`laxWhole`), which only cuts the file, but
    for what the head of Run/ParseLax.lean says that it refuses, reads it, and one check alone can
    refuse.
  `Toy1.Why`: which check of the page's verifier refuses a file, in the order of its checks: the
    work test; a spelling; the walk and the root; the file's end (too short, too long); the
    decision. (This is the order of the cases of `Toy1.Why`; `Toy1.why`, Fmt/Toy1.lean, tests "too
    short" earlier too: see its row there.)
  `Toy1.files`: all 21: name, bytes, and nothing for "accepted" or the check that refuses.

Limits: this file does not say that a verifier accepts or refuses them: Fmt/Toy1.lean.

Terms: lean/GLOSSARY.md.
-/
import Fmt.Rules23

namespace Fmt
namespace Toy1

/-- Which check refuses. -/
inductive Why where
  | work | spelling | walk | short | long | decision
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/-- The first honest file. -/
def honest : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- The second honest file. -/
def honest2 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- byte 0 of the random bytes, bit 0 flipped -/
def alt01 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- byte 0 of the root, bit 0 flipped -/
def alt02 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- the nonce 58 for 57: it FAILS the work test -/
def alt03 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- the nonce 310 for 57: the next one that PASSES the work test -/
def alt04 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- byte 0 of the column at 3, bit 0 flipped -/
def alt05 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- byte 0 of the salt at 3, bit 0 flipped -/
def alt06 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- byte 0 of the given digest (4, 2), bit 0 flipped -/
def alt07 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- byte 0 of s, bit 0 flipped -/
def alt08 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- the file one byte short -/
def alt09 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- the file one byte long (a zero byte behind it) -/
def alt10 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- the given digest (4, 2) and the given digest (4, 9) swapped -/
def alt11 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- EXTRA: the first word of the column at 3 is p (no spelling of an element) -/
def alt12 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- EXTRA: the first word of s is s_0 + p (the same element, another word) -/
def alt13 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- EXTRA: byte 0 of the random bytes flipped AND the nonce searched anew (52): the work test passes
-/
def alt14 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- EXTRA: byte 0 of the root flipped AND the nonce searched anew (175): the work test passes -/
def alt15 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- EXTRA: another row f (column 0 is (5, 5, 5)), all made by the rules, but s is one too large in
e_2: only the decision can refuse -/
def alt16 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- RE-CUT: the nonce 58, which FAILS the work test; opening and s made for the positions that it
draws [14, 5, 11], from the honest tree: only the work test can refuse -/
def alt17 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- RE-CUT: byte 0 of the root flipped, the least nonce anew (175), opening and s for the new
positions [4, 11, 6], from the honest tree: the walk ends in the honest root, not in the sent one -/
def alt18 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- RE-CUT: byte 0 of the random bytes flipped, the least nonce anew (52), opening and s for the new
positions [1, 1, 2], from the honest tree, whose leaves hold the OLD run's value: the walk does not
end in the root -/
def alt19 : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- All 21 files. -/
def files : List (String × ByteArray × Option Why) :=
  [("honest", honest, none), ("honest2", honest2, none),
   ("alt01", alt01, some .work),
   ("alt02", alt02, some .work),
   ("alt03", alt03, some .work),
   ("alt04", alt04, some .walk),
   ("alt05", alt05, some .walk),
   ("alt06", alt06, some .walk),
   ("alt07", alt07, some .walk),
   ("alt08", alt08, some .decision),
   ("alt09", alt09, some .short),
   ("alt10", alt10, some .long),
   ("alt11", alt11, some .walk),
   ("alt12", alt12, some .spelling),
   ("alt13", alt13, some .spelling),
   ("alt14", alt14, some .walk),
   ("alt15", alt15, some .walk),
   ("alt16", alt16, some .decision),
   ("alt17", alt17, some .work),
   ("alt18", alt18, some .walk),
   ("alt19", alt19, some .walk)]

-- the sizes
#guard files.map (fun x => x.2.1.size) = [512, 480, 512, 512, 512, 512, 512, 512, 512, 512, 511, 513, 512, 512, 512, 512, 512, 480, 512, 480, 352]
-- no two files are the same bytes
#guard (files.map fun x => hex x.2.1).eraseDups.length = 21
-- the digest of the first honest file, as the program that made it printed it
#guard hex (formatHash 168 0 0 zero32 honest) = "f1063f33eb2431b7cfa4038c83cb2cb460f1564c3b833115e24b6b91b24b3f3d"
-- these seven differ from the first honest file in one byte
#guard [alt01, alt02, alt03, alt05, alt06, alt07, alt08].all fun a => a.size = honest.size && ((List.range honest.size).filter fun i => byteAt a i != byteAt honest i).length = 1
-- the short file and the long file are the honest file but for their last byte
#guard alt09 = honest.extract 0 (honest.size - 1)
#guard alt10 = honest ++ zeroBytes 1

end Toy1
end Fmt
